Build snuffleupagus 0.14.0 instead of 0.12.0. 0.13 fixed CVE-2026-22034, a possible arbitrary code execution on misconfigured `upload_validation` deployments, and 0.14 fixed an opcache inlining issue that let calls bypass return-value rules. Mailu also imports 0.14's protections against `mb_send_mail` option injection and attacker-controlled `CURLOPT_SSLENGINE` values. Global strict mode remains enabled; the webmail SSO plugins now pass redirect status codes through `header()`'s third argument and set error status codes with `http_response_code()`, avoiding invalid implicit type coercions.
